--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFM Sm: bit bounds for register expressions from bounds on their atoms*: `exSm A s e`: every register, literal and `2^a` that `e` reads is at most `A` in absolute value,
--   and every divisor is positive. `exDg e` is a degree (sums add one, products add). Then
--   `|e.eval s| ≤ A^{exDg e}` (**`exSm_abs`**), and `A^{exDg e} < 2^B` gives `e.Bnd s B`
--   (**`exSm_bnd`**), which is the hypothesis of the RS cost lemmas.
